In the `interfaces` field, the pattern `"^.*$"` matches any string (i.e., any interface name). This is a bit of a catch-all, but it allows the schema to be more flexible.

In the `ip` field, the pattern `^(?:[0-9]{1,3}\\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}$` matches a standard IPv4 address. Here's a breakdown of the pattern:

- `^` matches the beginning of the string
- `(?:[0-9]{1,3}\\.){3}` matches exactly three groups of one to three digits followed by a period (`.`)
- `[0-9]{1,3}` matches one to three digits
